    {
      "type": "h1",
      "content": "Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Policy - Internal Use Only"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": "Effective Date: July 1, 2025. Version 4.0. This document outlines the guidelines and requirements for utilizing personal electronic devices for accessing Company resources, systems, and confidential data. Adherence to this policy is mandatory for all employees, contractors, and third-party vendors (collectively, 'Users') accessing corporate infrastructure. Non-compliance may result in disciplinary action, up to and including termination of access and employment."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": "1. Scope and Definitions"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": "This policy applies to all personally owned devices (smartphones, tablets, laptops, etc.) used for business purposes within the organization's ecosystem. 'Company Resources' includes, but is not limited to, policyholder data, proprietary underwriting models, internal communication channels, and financial records."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": "2. Acceptable Use Standards (AUS)"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": "Users must ensure their personal devices meet minimum security standards before deployment for business use. Key requirements include, but are not limited to: up-to-date operating system versions (within 90 days of release), strong biometric authentication, and functional anti-malware protection."
    },
    {
      "type": "ol",
      "items": [
        "Ensure all personal devices are enrolled in the Company's Mobile Device Management (MDM) system to facilitate remote wiping and security audits.",
        "Users are strictly prohibited from installing unauthorized applications or jailbreaking/rooting devices, as this compromises the integrity of the corporate connection.",
        "Data accessed via BYOD must be processed only through secured, corporate-mandated Virtual Private Network (VPN) tunnels.",
        "Encryption must be enabled on the device level for all stored data, aligning with industry best practices for sensitive information handling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": "3. Data Handling and Security Protocols"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": "The separation of personal and corporate data is paramount. Company data must never be transferred to non-corporate cloud services (e.g., personal photo backups, non-sanctioned file-sharing sites). Users must utilize the encrypted corporate container provided by the MDM solution for all work-related files."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Security Measure",
        "Requirement",
        "Compliance Metric"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Mandatory Data Encryption",
          "AES-256 Bit Standard",
          "99.9% Compliance Rate Observed (Q2 2025)"
        ],
        [
          "Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)",
          "Required for all system logins",
          "100% Adoption Target"
        ],
        [
          "Incident Reporting Timeline",
          "Immediate reporting (within 2 hours) of loss or theft",
          "Mean Time to Report (MTTR) < 2 hours"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "content": "4. Incident Response and Remediation"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": "In the event of a device loss, theft, or suspected compromise, the User must immediately notify their direct manager and the IT Security Department. The IT Security team retains the right, and reserves the right, to issue a remote wipe command to the enrolled device. Users must acknowledge and consent to the possibility of corporate data erasure upon device separation to mitigate risk exposure."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "content": "Failure to cooperate with security protocols, including non-compliance with MDM enrollment or delay in reporting incidents, will be deemed a breach of company policy and may result in immediate revocation of system access privileges."
    }
  ]
}

